Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:12:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] meson.build: add a docs option

The HTML API documentation is built whenever sphinx-build is found, so
whether a package build runs Sphinx depends on what happens to be
installed on the build host, and a packager cannot turn it off. The
output is not installed, so a distribution build only spends time on
it, and with -W any Sphinx warning fails the whole build.

Add a boolean "docs" option, true by default: Sphinx is used when
found, as before. With -Ddocs=false it is not looked up. As with the
"tests" option, a boolean rather than a feature keeps
--auto-features=enabled, as used by Fedora's %meson, from making Sphinx
a hard requirement.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N8fTR5eZWWPFd2fewTXKDt
Signed-off-by: Fco Javier Felix <ffelix@inode64.com>
---
 docs/meson.build  | 11 ++++++++---
 meson_options.txt |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/meson.build b/docs/meson.build
index fcb4503..892a7e7 100644
--- a/docs/meson.build
+++ b/docs/meson.build
@@ -2,10 +2,15 @@
 #
 # Copyright (C) 2026 Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab+huawei@kernel.org>
 
-sphinx = find_program('sphinx-build', required: false)
+enable_sphinx = false
+if get_option('docs')
+    sphinx = find_program('sphinx-build', required: false)
+    enable_sphinx = sphinx.found()
+endif
 
-enable_sphinx = sphinx.found()
-if not enable_sphinx
+if not get_option('docs')
+    message('Documentation build disabled')
+elif not enable_sphinx
     message('Sphinx not found. Skipping documentation build')
 else
     sphinx_sources += [
diff --git a/meson_options.txt b/meson_options.txt
index 142f1eb..f43d3c2 100644
--- a/meson_options.txt
+++ b/meson_options.txt
@@ -8,6 +8,9 @@
 option('disable-all', type : 'boolean', value: false,
         description: 'disable all features. Useful to check broken deps')
 
+option('docs', type : 'boolean', value : true,
+       description : 'build the HTML API documentation when Sphinx is found')
+
 option('enable-arch', type : 'combo', choices : ['auto', 'all', 'x86', 'arm', 'riscv'],
        value : 'all',
        description : 'select the architecture-specific event family (or all for testing)')
